# [Perf] [AMD] qwen: Fuse decode FP8 quant into GDN norm and output gate
# https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/51023  (PR head 68aa5f41d2)
# Generated against the 20261117 image's SGLang checkout (c67db7c762) with patches 01-07, 09, 11, 13-16, 21, 24, 23 and
# 26 applied; source files only (tests and the benchmark dropped).
# No variable: on aiter and gfx950, a Quark per-channel FP8 out_proj or o_proj with per-token activations at 1-256
# tokens (BF16) gets its (fp8, scale) pair from the launch before it (the GDN gated RMSNorm, the attention output
# gate, Qwen4-exp's included). The codes and scales equal the linear's own quant bit for bit; where a launch cannot
# round as the unfused one does (GDN head counts that are not a power of two below a token floor), the norm and the
# quant stay two launches.
# Port: unchanged; it applies with offsets on patch 24 (sglang#51180), which edits qwen4_exp.py.
# Apply in /sgl-workspace/sglang with git apply.

